THOUGHT: `compiler` is annotated @Nullable and may not be set before `renderInternal` is called, so dereferencing it directly causes the NullAway error. The safest fix is to add an explicit null check in `renderInternal` that throws an informative IllegalStateException if `compiler` is null, and then use a local non-null variable for compilation. I’ll modify the method accordingly and then run the NullAway build to ensure the error count decreases by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/spring-boot && sed -i '86,96s/^/	/' spring-boot-project/spring-boot/src/main/java/org/springframework/boot/web/reactive/result/view/MustacheView.java && sed -i '82,99c\ 	@Override
	protected Mono<Void> renderInternal(Map<String, Object> model, MediaType contentType, ServerWebExchange exchange) {
		Resource resource = resolveResource();
		if (resource == null) {
			return Mono
					.error(new IllegalStateException("Could not find Mustache template with URL [" + getUrl() + "]"));
		}
		Compiler compiler = this.compiler;
		if (compiler == null) {
			return Mono.error(new IllegalStateException("Mustache Compiler must not be null"));
		}
		DataBuffer dataBuffer = exchange.getResponse().bufferFactory()
				.allocateBuffer(DefaultDataBufferFactory.DEFAULT_INITIAL_CAPACITY);
		try (Reader reader = getReader(resource)) {
			Template template = compiler.compile(reader);
			Charset charset = getCharset(contentType).orElseGet(this::getDefaultCharset);
			try (Writer writer = new OutputStreamWriter(dataBuffer.asOutputStream(), charset)) {
				template.execute(model, writer);
				writer.flush();
			}
		}
		catch (Exception ex) {
			DataBufferUtils.release(dataBuffer);
			return Mono.error(ex);
		}
		return exchange.getResponse().writeWith(Flux.just(dataBuffer));
	}
